          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? So a rhombus is a parallelogram, and a rectangle is also a parallelogram. How can this be represented using a Venn diagram?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.391,
            0.672,
            0.414
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Where will the set of squares occur in this diagram?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.416,
            0.848,
            0.492
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We know that a square is a rectangle. Since the opposite sides of a square are parallel, a square is also a parallelogram. Further, since all the sides of a square have the same length, a square is also a rhombus. Thus, the Venn diagram will be as follows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.496,
            0.903,
            0.704
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.118,
                0.496,
                0.903,
                0.704
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_19_image_9.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.717,
            0.532,
            0.738
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us list the properties of a rhombus."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.741,
            0.761,
            0.763
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Property 1:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " All the sides of a rhombus are equal to each other."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.766,
            0.843,
            0.788
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Property 2:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The opposite sides of a rhombus are parallel to each other."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.791,
            0.848,
            0.831
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Property 3:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " In a rhombus, the adjacent angles add up to 180°, and the opposite angles are equal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
